On 2026-10-16, an authorized canonical image append stopped during its
verification baseline, before opening a question editor or uploading bytes.
A native Edit Info read received HTTP 429 with a Cloudflare response, while
an independently spaced native read succeeded with HTTP 200. The opener is
a server action even though the product only reads metadata and cancels.

The companion now serializes metadata read jobs and leaves five seconds
between completed attempts within the original eight-second read budget.
This is a conservative local pacing policy, not a verified provider limit;
it neither retries failed actions nor changes mutation receipts.

Deterministic
regressions cover overlapping jobs, deadlines and interrupted waits. Live
image acceptance remains pending.

Cloudflare's [HTTP 429 reference][metadata-rate-doc], checked on 2026-10-16,
confirms that this status represents rate limiting and that Retry-After may
be supplied. The observed response did not supply that header; Cloudflare API
quota numbers are unrelated to Blooket and were not adopted.

